{"label": "4567ce82296f9cfad744", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "own_sincere", "referents": [{"word": "them", "refers_to": "transactions", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}, {"word": "their", "refers_to": "people/nobody (generic)", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}], "conditions": [], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "Nobody denominates their transactions in Bitcoin; they denominate them in dollars, in Bitcoin's worth of dollars.", "certainty": "certain", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "I'm sure you're going to say that taxation is theft and the government is robbing us all. That's fine. I am trying to explain how the system functions."},
{"label": "5d5e163125435e85061a", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "conditional", "referents": [], "conditions": [{"text": "if you want to have confidence that any purchases of Bitcoin are going to be legal", "inside": true}], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "To have confidence that purchases of Bitcoin for the Strategic Reserve are legal, authorization from Congress, which controls the purse strings, would be needed.", "certainty": "certain", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "So by that, you mean an executive order is not robust enough on its own. This needs to be in law in some way. Yes."},
{"label": "5e38ec62aa36eae80132", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "own_sincere", "referents": [{"word": "it", "refers_to": "Bitcoin", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}], "conditions": [{"text": "all it has to do is stay decentralized and secure", "inside": true}], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "Bitcoin is a new system of measure for the first free market ever, and it only needs to stay decentralized and secure for that to emerge.", "certainty": "certain", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "why that's interesting for this conversation to your initial question is how could we superimpose those two thoughts on what's going on right now?"},
{"label": "6353ef6c32236e89f0cc", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "conditional", "referents": [], "conditions": [{"text": "even if you have Bitcoin as a standard", "inside": true}], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "Even with a Bitcoin standard, speculators would still issue liabilities denominated in Bitcoin, so somebody will always be issuing some kind of loan.", "certainty": "certain", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "Look, I'm not defending wars or governments bailing out banks. I have written about this, explicitly opposed this."},
{"label": "d1e31dd4b7ddb686a18d", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "own_sincere", "referents": [{"word": "it", "refers_to": "using Bitcoin privately via e-cash / this freedom tech", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}], "conditions": [], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "You can now use Bitcoin completely privately, pegged one-to-one in e-cash with private money and communications, and most of the world doesn't know it already exists, just as the world didn't know what the dawn of the internet would bring.", "certainty": "certain", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "So where do you see like the next, I don't know, 10, 20 years? Because you're always someone who says you don't focus on the Fiat price."},
{"label": "e8c3738e3d7aff4ba06e", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "own_sincere", "referents": [], "conditions": [], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "It's been concluded that Bitcoin broke the stock-to-flow model to the downside because that model, which charted the inverse of Bitcoin's supply and inflation rate, was too bullish.", "certainty": "certain", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "So I guess first offer a quick explanation, like what is this Bitcoin power law stuff? And then explain for us why you think the power law could break in Bitcoin. Yeah, absolutely. I mean,"},
{"label": "0c751a33022013fb3086", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "own_sincere", "referents": [{"word": "it", "refers_to": "Bitcoin", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}], "conditions": [], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "In markets, everyone loves Bitcoin in a hot bull market and hates it in a bear market, which is why the price got high at the top and low at the bottom.", "certainty": "certain", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "And I think when you get more people involved, things can change in possibly the wrong direction at the wrong time. And like, that's the nature of markets."},
{"label": "316f66f81603ea55899a", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "conditional", "referents": [{"word": "it", "refers_to": "Bitcoin", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}, {"word": "it", "refers_to": "the cycle of creating dollar credit to buy Bitcoin", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}], "conditions": [{"text": "if the price of Bitcoin goes higher", "inside": true}], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "If Bitcoin's price goes higher it becomes better collateral allowing more dollar credit, and this could be sustainable because Bitcoin is perfectly scarce while the dollar, which is continually created by design, is not.", "certainty": "likely", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "I think with that context, it's kind of like, all right, we're able to create more and more dollar credit."}
]}
